# Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
artifacts/
# Any local publish directory. Broadened from publish/ + publish-test*/ so a new
# verification build (publish-verify/, etc.) cannot be committed by accident.
publish*/

# IDE
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# Test output
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
coverage*

# Local tooling / scratch
_temp/
_tools/__pycache__/

# Internal working notes — NOT published.
#
# These contain candid career material: direct quotes about how gaps in the CV might be
# read, notes on what is not remembered, framing strategy, and (in earlier revisions) a
# colleague's medical detail. They stay on disk and remain readable locally; they are
# simply never committed to the public repository.
docs/content/
docs/superpowers/
#
# Loose notes dropped straight into docs/ were caught by name one at a time, which only
# ever worked for files that already existed: plan.md and resume-prompt.md landed here
# later and were tracked by nothing, so `git add .` would have published them. Ignore the
# whole top level instead. Subdirectories are unaffected, which is what keeps the two
# genuinely published trees — docs/writeups/ and docs/screenshots/ — committable.
/docs/*.md

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Seeded design canvas output (regenerated from design/*.dc.html)
design/portfolio-landing-page.html

# Superseded source CVs. Kept locally for reference; never published — they carry
# an old phone number and content that output/ now supersedes.
/resume 2-9-26.pdf
/Bahaa Aldeen Mohamed.pdf
